$\begin{align*}P(2<X<5)&=\int_2^5\frac{3x^2}{215}\,dx\\&=\left[\frac{x^3}{215}\right]_2^5\\&=\frac{125-8}{215}\\&=\frac{117}{215}\end{align*}$
The shaded region represents this probability. Including either endpoint gives the same probability because $P(X=2)=P(X=5)=0$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=45mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{probblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{probfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[probfill] (2,0) -- plot[domain=2:5,samples=50,variable=\x] ({\x},{3*(\x)*(\x)/215}) -- (5,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,->] (0,0) -- (6.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,0) -- (0,0.68) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[probblue,thick] plot[domain=1:6,samples=70,variable=\x] ({\x},{3*(\x)*(\x)/215});
\draw[black,dashed] (1,0) -- (1,{3/215});
\draw[black,dashed] (6,0) -- (6,{108/215});
\draw[black] (2,0) -- (2,{12/215});
\draw[black] (5,0) -- (5,{75/215});
\foreach \v in {1,2,5,6}{\draw[black] (\v,0) -- (\v,-0.025);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\v,-0.025) {$\v$};}
\node[above left] at (5.9,{3*5.9*5.9/215}) {$f(x)=\frac{3x^2}{215}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
